            <ArticleTitle>Prevalence of chronic knee pain in children and adolescents in northern Finland.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>803-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A questionnaire was sent to 967 schoolchildren, in two age groups, in northern Finland in order to investigate the prevalence of chronic knee pain. A response rate of 88.5% was achieved. Adolescents (aged 14-15 years) had significantly more knee pain (p &lt; 0.0001) than children (aged 9-10 years). The total prevalence of chronic knee pain at the time of the evaluation was 18.5% among adolescents and 3.9% among children. There was no significant difference in the prevalence of chronic knee pain between boys and girls in these age groups. Overweight was not a predisposing factor in chronic knee pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
